      "costUsd": 0.008148500000000001,
      "pronunciationText": "Last video ended with this flat density, from one to five. We'll find its height soon. First, here's where flat densities come from. A bus comes every ten minutes, and you turn up at a random moment, so every point in the ten-minute gap is equally likely. How long will you wait? Let's simulate two hundred arrivals, and sort their waits into one-minute classes. The bars come out roughly level. Any wait from zero to ten minutes can happen, and no stretch of waiting times is more likely than another of the same width. So what does the density look like? And how tall is it?"
    },
    {
