      "successfulRequestCount": 1,
      "loggedRequestAttempts": 1,
      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 110,
      "outputTokens": 883,
      "costUsd": 0.008001999999999999,
      "pronunciationText": "Equally likely has a precise meaning here. Take any two intervals of the same width, say from one to three minutes and from six to eight. They must carry the same probability. Slide a window of width two anywhere within zero to ten, and its probability can't change. On a density, probability is area. So equal widths with equal areas means equal heights. The density has to be flat: a constant height c, from zero to ten, and zero outside, because a wait below zero or above ten can't happen."
    },
