      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 108,
      "outputTokens": 894,
      "costUsd": 0.0081,
      "pronunciationText": "Now, how tall? The total area under any density is one. Here the area is a rectangle, ten wide and c tall, so ten times c equals one, and c is one tenth. That height means a tenth of the probability per minute: each minute of the interval holds a tenth of the total. The same works on any interval from a to b. The rectangle is b minus a wide, so its height must be one over b minus a. We didn't choose that height. Total probability one forced it."
    },
