      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 128,
      "outputTokens": 881,
      "costUsd": 0.007993,
      "pronunciationText": "So what's the chance you wait less than four minutes? That's the area from zero to four. It's four wide and one tenth tall, which is zero point four. And between three and seven minutes? Also four wide, so also zero point four. For a uniform model, a probability is just the fraction of the interval that's covered. Where the interval sits doesn't matter, only its width. It's the same idea on any interval. If X is uniform from two to ten, the whole width is eight. So the chance X is between four and seven is three eighths."
    },
