      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 141,
      "outputTokens": 1009,
      "costUsd": 0.0091515,
      "pronunciationText": "What about the cumulative distribution function? Back at the bus stop, F of t is the area to the left of t. As t moves right, the area grows by the same amount every minute, because the height never changes. So F climbs in a straight line, from zero at the start to one at the end. On any interval from a to b, F of x is x minus a, over b minus a. Before a it stays at zero, and after b it stays at one. You can check this with an integral too. F of x is the integral from a to x of one over b minus a, which gives the same x minus a, over b minus a."
    },
