      "inputTokens": 154,
      "outputTokens": 1126,
      "costUsd": 0.010211000000000001,
      "pronunciationText": "Now back to the flat density from one to five. Say it's the time a train waits at a platform, uniform between one and five minutes. The interval is four wide, so the density is one quarter from one to five, and zero elsewhere. Then F of t is the integral of a quarter from one up to t, which is t minus one, over four. The chance the train waits more than three and a half minutes is one minus F of three and a half. That's one minus two point five over four, which is zero point three seven five. And the chance it waits between two and four minutes is three quarters minus one quarter, a half. That's two of the four minutes, so a half makes sense."
    },
