      "pronunciationText": "This should feel familiar. A fair die spreads a total probability of one equally over six values, so each gets one sixth. A continuous uniform spreads it evenly over an interval, so its height is one over the width. And because the density is flat, no value is higher than any other. So a uniform distribution has no single mode."
